## Why This Question Is Asked
This evaluates your ability to validate a production-grade streaming ML pipeline under realistic conditions, covering data integrity, performance under load, drift handling, and safe deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end streaming test strategies and synthetic data generation
- Backpressure handling and consumer lag in Kafka/Flink
- Feature drift detection and model retraining triggers
- Canary rollouts, shadow traffic, and safe rollback procedures

## Code Example
```javascript
// End-to-end test harness wiring synthetic replay, latency tracking,
// and assertion validation
async function runE2ETest(config) {
  const syntheticData = generateLabeledAnomalies(config);
  const results = await pipeline.process(syntheticData);

  const latency = measureLatency(results);
  assert(latency.p95 < 300, 'P95 latency exceeded budget');
  assert(latency.p99 < 1000, 'P99 latency exceeded budget');

  const correctness = validateChecksums(results);
  assert(correctness, 'Data correctness check failed');

  return { latency, correctness };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Real-time pipelines present subtle consistency and resilience challenges that unit tests alone cannot catch. Interviewers want to see that you understand end-to-end testing across distributed systems, including CI/CD integration.

## Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics via transactional sinks and checkpointing
- Stateful stream processing and its failure modes
- Backward/forward schema evolution to prevent consumer breakage
- Backpressure handling, failure recovery, and replay safety
- Observability within CI/CD pipelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify exactly-once processing with idempotent writes
const result = await warehouse.query(`
  SELECT event_id, COUNT(*) as score_count
  FROM risk_scores
  GROUP BY event_id
  HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
`);
assert(result.length === 0, 'Duplicate events detected');

// Validate replay safety after simulated outage
await kafka.broker.crash({ node: 3 });
await flink.restartFromCheckpoint();
const postRecoveryScores = await warehouse.fetchLatestScores();
assert(postRecoveryScores.length === expectedCount);
```

